    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "page": 2,
      "section_path": [
        "4. First-Aid Measures"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "4. First-Aid Measures"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "page": 2,
      "section_path": [
        "4. First-Aid Measures"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "text": "FIRST AID - EYE CONTACT: Immediately flush eyes with plenty of water for at least 15 minutes holding eyelids open. Get medical\nattention. Do NOT allow rubbing of eyes or keeping eyes closed.\nFIRST AID - SKIN CONTACT: Wash skin with soap and water. Remove contaminated clothing. Get medical attention if irritation\ndevelops or persists.\nFIRST AID - INHALATION: Remove to fresh air. If not breathing, give artificial respiration. If breathing is difficult, give oxygen. Get\nimmediate medical attention. Do NOT use mouth-to-mouth resuscitation. If you experience difficulty in breathing, leave the area to\nobtain fresh air. If continued difficulty is experienced, get medical assistance immediately.\nFIRST AID - INGESTION: Swallowing less than an ounce will not cause significant harm. For larger amounts, do not induce\nvomiting, but give one or two glasses of water to drink and get medical attention. If swallowed, rinse mouth with water. If feeling\nunwell, get medical attention."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "page": 2,
      "section_path": [
        "5. Fire-Fighting Measures"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "5. Fire-Fighting Measures"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "page": 2,
      "section_path": [
        "5. Fire-Fighting Measures"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "text": "EXTINGUISHING MEDIA: None Known"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "page": 2,
      "section_path": [
        "5. Fire-Fighting Measures"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "text": "UNUSUAL FIRE AND EXPLOSION HAZARDS: No unusual fire or explosion hazards noted. Keep containers tightly closed. FLASH\nPOINT IS TESTED TO BE GREATER THAN 200 DEGREES F.\nSPECIAL FIREFIGHTING PROCEDURES: Water may be used to cool closed containers to prevent buildup of steam. If water is\nused, fog nozzles are preferred."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "page": 2,
      "section_path": [
        "5. Fire-Fighting Measures",
        "Special Fire and Explosion Hazard (Combustible Dust): No Information"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "level": 4,
      "text": "Special Fire and Explosion Hazard (Combustible Dust): No Information"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "page": 2,
      "section_path": [
        "6. Accidental Release Measures"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "6. Accidental Release Measures"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "page": 2,
      "section_path": [
        "6. Accidental Release Measures"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "text": "STEPS TO BE TAKEN IF MATERIAL IS RELEASED OR SPILLED: If spilled, contain spilled material and remove with inert\nabsorbent. Dispose of contaminated absorbent, container, and unused contents in accordance with local, state, and federal\nregulations. Do not incinerate closed containers"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "page": 2,
      "section_path": [
        "7. Handling and Storage"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "7. Handling and Storage"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "page": 2,
      "section_path": [
        "7. Handling and Storage"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "text": "HANDLING: Wash thoroughly after handling. Wash hands before eating. Remove contaminated clothing and launder before reuse.\nUse only with adequate ventilation. Follow all SDS and label precautions even after container is emptied because it may retain\nproduct residues. Avoid breathing fumes, vapors, or mist. Avoid contact with eyes, skin and clothing.\nSTORAGE: Store in a dry, well ventilated place. Keep container tightly closed when not in use."
    },
