    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "page": 3,
      "section_path": [
        "8. Exposure Controls / Personal Protection",
        "PERSONAL PROTECTION"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "level": 4,
      "text": "PERSONAL PROTECTION"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "page": 3,
      "section_path": [
        "8. Exposure Controls / Personal Protection",
        "PERSONAL PROTECTION"
      ],
      "zone": "main",
      "text": "ENGINEERING CONTROLS: Use process enclosures, local exhaust ventilation, or other engineering controls to control airborne\nlevels below recommended exposure limits. Prevent build-up of vapors by opening all doors and windows to achieve cross-\nventilation.\nRESPIRATORY PROTECTION: A respiratory protection program that meets OSHA 1910.134 and ANSI Z88.2 requirements must be\nfollowed whenever workplace conditions warrant a respirator's use.\nSKIN PROTECTION: Use gloves to prevent prolonged skin contact. Nitrile or Neoprene gloves may afford adequate skin protection.\nEYE PROTECTION: Use safety eyewear designed to protect against splash of liquids.\nOTHER PROTECTIVE EQUIPMENT: Refer to safety supervisor or industrial hygienist for further guidance regarding types of\npersonal protective equipment and their applications.\nHYGIENIC PRACTICES: Wash thoroughly with soap and water before eating, drinking or smoking. Remove contaminated clothing\nimmediately and launder before reuse."
    },
